    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Property Partners Gill & Glynn are pleased to bring to market this substantial detached, turn-key family residence, occupying a generous and private site of approximately 0.85 acres. \n\nLocated in the townland of Barnaderag, between the villages of Abbeyknockmoy (5.3km) and Moylough (9.2km). The property is situated c. 14km from Mountbellew, just 15km from Tuam Town and 36km from Galway City, offering buyers the benefits of countryside living while remaining within reach of larger towns and Galway City. While Athenry train station is just a 20 minute drive. \n\nConstructed in 2009 and extending to approximately 263 sq. m. (3,153 sq. ft.), and accommodation is spread over three floors. The property was constructed to a high standard to include, natural slate, hollow core flooring, quality woodwork including solid mahogany doors and solid wood kitchen. \n\nThis impressive home offers spacious and versatile accommodation, with five bedrooms, (2 ensuites) a superb selection of living areas, a playroom and home office, ideally suited to modern family life.\n\nThe property boasts an energy efficient B2 BER rating, making it eligible for green` finance. The property benefits from a dual heating system including oil-fired boiler and solid fuel range with radiator central heating together with solar panels for hot water.\n\nACCOMMODATION\n\nThe property opens into an impressive bright and spacious entrance hallway from which the principal ground-floor accommodation is accessed. At the heart of the home is a bespoke open-plan kitchen, dining and family living area. The country-style fitted kitchen provides an extensive range of cabinetry and storage together with generous worktop space and a large central island. A traditional solid fuel range forms an attractive focal point within the kitchen and benefits from a back boiler.\n\nThe adjoining dining area is positioned beside double doors opening directly onto the garden, allowing plenty of natural light into this spacious family area.\n\nThe kitchen and dining accommodation flows into the conservatory area offering further living space. \n\nA separate sitting room provides a more formal reception area. Finished in rich tones and featuring timber flooring, an open fireplace and attractive bay window, this is a warm and comfortable room ideal for entertaining or relaxing.\n\nThe ground floor also includes a generously proportioned ensuite bedroom, providing valuable flexibility for guests. A utility room and separate WC complete the ground-floor accommodation.\n\nThe first floor comprises four well-proportioned bedrooms and a family bathroom. The master bedroom benefits from an ensuite and a walk-in wardrobe. The remaining bedrooms offer excellent family accommodation, and the main bathroom serves this floor also.\n\nThe second floor comprises of two further rooms which could be used as a home office, playroom or additional storage. \n\n(See floor plan provided)\n\nThe property occupies a site of approximately 0.85 acres, approached through gated access onto an extensive tarmacadam driveway providing ample parking.\n\nA particularly valuable feature is the substantial block-built double garage, complete with two roller doors, providing excellent secure parking, storage or workshop space.\n\n\nLarge lawns extend around the residence, complemented by established boundary hedging and landscaped planting. A paved patio area to the rear provides additional outdoor space.\n\n\nVIEWING\n\nContact: Claire Glynn at Property Partners Gill & Glynn today by phone, email or WhatsApp on; P: 091 884000 / 087 9655584\n\n\nAttention is drawn to this important notice. \n\n\nProperty Partners Gill & Glynn for themselves and for the vendors or lessors of this property whose agents they are, give notice that:\n\n(i) The particulars are set out as a general outline for the guidance of intending purchasers or lessees, and do not constitute, nor constitute part of, an offer or contract. \n(ii) All descriptions, dimensions, references to condition and necessary permissions for use and occupation, and other details are given in good faith and are believed to be correct, but any intending purchasers or tenants should not rely on them as statements or representations of fact but must satisfy themselves by inspection or otherwise as to the correctness of each of them. \n(iii) We have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. \n(iv) All measurements are approximate and photographs and maps provided are for guidance only.\n"
      },
